      "message": "Usually we do break the loop on the error conditions. I didn\u0027t really get why the original author didn\u0027t do this. Could this be because that we are not really caring this error return value when kswapd thread is failed to run? (even in the upstream implementations we are not really caring if kswapd thread really started running in the system. grepping the kswapd_run() shows this). What if only 1 in N kswapd threads can fail to spawn? with early breaking the loop we may loose the other threads. NO?",
