      "writtenOn": "2021-02-16T20:29:10Z",
      "side": 1,
      "message": "One issue with this approach is if the pgdat-\u003emkswapd[0] fails to start but some other threads succeed. In that scenario pgdat-\u003ekswapd will be NULL, so another call to kswapd_run() will try to restart all kthreads again, so we might end up with more than MAX_KSWAPD_THREADS active kswapd threads.\nI think this issue can be dealt with by setting pgdat-\u003ekswapd to the first kthread that got successfully started instead of doing pgdat-\u003ekswapd \u003d pgdat-\u003emkswapd[0].",
      "parentUuid": "28b66735_13ebf2bf",
